From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:54:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tests/color-management: Cover CTA and base EDID display
 targets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cover the declared targets of outputs off the native DisplayID route
end to end, each in its own invocation since both rewrite the fixture
output:

 - an external monitor declaring only CTA-861 HDR static metadata, a
   desired maximum of 600 and a desired minimum of 0.05 cd/m², and base
   EDID primaries, in BT.2100: its luminance target carries CTA
   provenance, is published as 0.05 to 600 cd/m², and is carried by the
   blending state, while its target gamut stays the BT.2020 fallback;
   PQ content mastered at 1000 cd/m² is highlight mapped toward 600 and
   refused direct scanout. Without a desired maximum, with one at the
   reference white, and with HDR forced, the luminance target is the
   fallback;
 - a wide gamut panel whose white point is not D65, in the native SDR
   mode: its target primaries equal its encoding primaries with EDID
   provenance; its own encoding and content in its published
   colorimetry are not mapped and may be scanned out; BT.2020 content
   is compressed toward the panel's gamut while sRGB content is not;
   the default SDR mode and unusable base primaries keep the fallback in
   both modes.

A new client mode compares the published output description with the
values the compositor expects.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
